# Secrets. The gatekeeper's signing key IS the business: anyone holding it can
# mint entitlements, and because the public half is the contract's parameters,
# replacing it moves the contract to a different address and abandons every
# envelope already sold. The content keys open the catalogue.
keys/
node_modules/
target/

# Generated by catalog/build.py and ui/, from sources that ARE tracked.
site/enc/
site/posters/
site/catalog.json
site/config.json
site/app.js
site/index.html
site/style.css
tests/fixtures/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# decrypted output — regenerated by `catflix order`, and it is the plaintext
unlocked/

# Regenerated every sweep. `keys/` is the one that must never be deleted.
run/

# The payer's Rust build output. `target/` above already matches this, but it
# is named explicitly because the pattern above was written for the contract
# crates at the repository root and a reader should not have to work out that
# it reaches here too. The SOURCE is tracked; `cargo build --release` in
# payer/ootle/toolkit rebuilds the binary agent_wallet.py looks for.
payer/ootle/toolkit/target/
